 class=3D"ud-text-md rt-scaffolding" id=3D"overall-explanation"><p>Correct =
option:</p>

<p><strong>Backup and restore strategy</strong></p>

<p>When selecting your DR strategy, you must weigh the benefits of lower re=
covery time objective (RTO) and recovery point objective (RPO) vs the costs=
 of implementing and operating a strategy. The Backup and restore strategy =
offers a good balance of benefits and cost for the current use case. This i=
s the cheapest of all the disaster recovery options available with AWS.</p>

<p>Backup and restore is the most suitable approach for the given use case =
as the university can tolerate data loss of a few hours. This approach can =
be used to mitigate against a regional disaster by replicating data to othe=
r AWS Regions or to mitigate the lack of redundancy for workloads deployed =
to a single Availability Zone. In addition to data, you must redeploy the i=
nfrastructure, configuration, and application code in the recovery Region.<=
/p>

<p>Comparing different disaster recovery strategies:
